  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Emily bought $1$ foot of gold wire and paid $\\$5.60$ for it. What's the unit price per yard?\n\nAssume that there are $3$ feet in one yard.",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that there are $3$ feet in each yard.  \n\nSince the price is $\\$5.60$ per foot, to find the price per yard, we multiply by $3:$\n\n$$\n5.60\\times 3=16.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gold wire costs $\\$16.80$ per yard.",
